      "note": "The seated figure holds its right hand in abhaya mudra; the museum interprets the gesture as approachability."
    },
    {
      "id": "met-text:38198:gesture",
      "sourceId": "met-text",
      "url": "https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection/search/38198",
      "retrievedAt": "2026-10-28T20:28:42Z",
      "locator": "Overview, first paragraph, sentence describing the missing right hand",
      "note": "The museum identifies the figure's original gesture as abhaya mudra. The right hand is now missing; the gesture is a curatorial reconstruction, not visible intact anatomy."
    },
    {
      "id": "met-text:neo-definition",
      "sourceId": "met-text",
      "url": "https://www.metmuseum.org/essays/georges-seurat-1859-1891-and-neo-impressionism",
      "retrievedAt": "2026-10-28T20:28:42Z",
      "locator": "Dita Amory, October 2004; first body paragraph and paragraph about the 1886 exhibition",
      "note": "Amory describes Neo-Impressionism as flourishing principally in France during 1886–1906, led by Seurat, and identifies the Chicago painting as a defining example. This is one sourced movement definition."
    },
    {
      "id": "met-text:72381:production",
